{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1505325-how-you-use-the-totens","id":1505325,"title":"How you use the totens?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-14T10:21:09-07:00","id":1505325,"title":"How you use the totens?","content":"Packs can have totems that give them advantages, for a price, however I was curious, if the ideal is to use them only as resources or if it is possible that they can interact more directly in the chronicle, giving advice or instigating the characters to do something or as an occasional antagonist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T10:30:16-07:00","id":1505326,"title":"","content":"In practice I found most gaming groups use them only as mechanical benefits. Players tend to forget the totem is there. However, as ST I try to run them as a spirit NPC that is available for them to interact. Then it becomes an issue of where &quot;physically&quot; in the Penumbra the totem is at - most players tend to assume the pack totem will always be at the place where they decide to enter the Penumbra. They forget it is not a disembodied spirit, but has an actual form in the Umbra that moves. So players usually need some time to adjust to the idea of the spirit being an NPC.<br /> <br /> However, one issue is that players want to use the pack totems then as sources of advice (i.e. how to solve the plot the ST has put in front of us) which defeats the purpose of the ST running the plot to players. They are supposed to figure that out themselves. So it is important the ST does not allow the pack totem to know anything more than what the players do except for some basic information about the umbra or general setting information.<br /> <br /> Of course the ST can decide to use them as a means to introduce the plot to the PCs. That's just as valid as using Mentors, Allies calling in favors, the sept leadership, etc. doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T13:45:50-07:00","id":1505372,"title":"","content":"Totems tend to be picked for the mechanical benefits - and there is a lot of them to pick from and build up.<br /> <br /> However, what this tends to miss is the fact that the Totems are an amazing narrative tool. First of all, they are a character and one that grows with the pack over time. They become more powerful and their outlooks and preferences are shaped by the pack, just as the pack is shaped by its preferences.<br /> <br /> Secondly, the Totem binds the pack on an instinctual and emotional level - it allows them to coordinate in battle, but also to feel each other and how the others are doing and if they need each other. Any group under a pack has a connection deeper than that of a family as they all participate in the Totem bond. This allows the pack to smooth over differences and have an impartial mediator.<br /> <br /> Thirdly the Totem has mixed loyalties. Sure, it's loyal to the pack, but it's also a facet of a more powerful Incarna and as such it may have orders or allegiances that can conflict with the characters. Combining that with point two makes for excellent drama.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T15:54:51-07:00","id":1505381,"title":"","content":"IME a lot of people treat them as stat boosts. It's something I don't get because even if you don't care about the spirituality and story potential involved with everything that goes into a pack's relationship with their spirit... the pack has this spirit that they're allied with and for very little XP relatively to returns, can be extremely potent. Even from a pure optimization standpoint, jacking up your Totems Rage/Gnosis/Willpower (and thus Essence) and Charms is really cheap, as is taking the benefit that they're always nearby... the players can build their spirit towards all sorts of things that the pack might want more help with.<br /> <br /> In my groups, we tend to love making them more of a part of the game because there's so much more to them. Neglecting them like I've seen so many people do just baffles me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T16:15:34-07:00","id":1505384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1505325-how-you-use-the-totens?p=1505381#post1505381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IME a lot of people treat them as stat boosts. It's something I don't get because even if you don't care about the spirituality and story potential involved with everything that goes into a pack's relationship with their spirit... the pack has this spirit that they're allied with and for very little XP relatively to returns, can be extremely potent. Even from a pure optimization standpoint, jacking up your Totems Rage/Gnosis/Willpower (and thus Essence) and Charms is really cheap, as is taking the benefit that they're always nearby... the players can build their spirit towards all sorts of things that the pack might want more help with.<br /> <br /> In my groups, we tend to love making them more of a part of the game because there's so much more to them. Neglecting them like I've seen so many people do just baffles me.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my group the players have been avoiding them lately (in Ahadi and KotE) as they feel they might expose personal secrets or end up too much of a responsibility, so I guess I may have overdone something <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T20:13:45-07:00","id":1508814,"title":"","content":"I like to make some perks to affect the pack too as a houserule to incentivize them to stay with the totem throughout the chronicle and grow with them. Using the flavor text of the totem as the basis. For example: bear is known for healing and mysticism, also for being a war totem. When all pack achieves Rank 2 I make a bonus of +3 Occult to be a pack trait. When all are at Rank 3 I make the Mother's Touch use given by the bear doesn't require Gnosis (if they learn the Gift itself I turn it into 2 charges per day). When all are at Rank 4 I give them +1 Stamina as an individual trait.When all are at Rank 5 I give them Huge Size Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T21:07:48-07:00","id":1508829,"title":"","content":"Totems were always described as a true member of a pack, so I it that way. It is an npc that is either present in the umbra, or show it's influence in the material world. <br /> <br /> It's also a good prompt for interactions between packs, such as distrust when your totem are not the best friends possible.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor exemple, my current players have Owl as a pack totem. Everytime they travel at night, they hear owls screetching at them as a salutation. They also discovered that silent striders are now more open with them, but had a very rought introduction with a pack of bones gnawers, because, well, Owl and Rat.<br /> <br /> Another NPC pack had a spiritnI made, &quot;Glitch&quot; which is the manifestation of system collapsing. People's phone and computers had short bugs when a member of the pack was around, and the totem pushed them to do small acts of sabotage when using tech.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T23:32:10-07:00","id":1508847,"title":"","content":"That interpretation does somewhat devalue some of the bonuses you can buy for your pack's Totem customization; the implication is that, unless the pack dedicates some Totem points in that direction, the spirit would not generally be around the pack all the time and instead tend to hang out somewhere more natural to it in the Umbra. Though considering Septs made it a habit of having shrines to the pack totems on Sept land, that would mean most packs wouldn't have trouble interacting with their patron when &quot;at home.&quot;<br /> <br /> The individual write-ups also use alterations to social perceptions as part of the base Totem package. Owl packs are supposed to have an easier time with Silent Striders and a harder time with Bone Gnawers because that's part of taking Owl as your Totem. Most pack totem spirits aren't going to result in prompts like that because most don't care enough (and spirit politics can be really complicated). Overdoing these sorts of default social stressors makes it weird for the ones the books call out as special.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}